## 3. Implementation Plan

**Steps & Timeline**

| Phase | Work | Status / Timing |
|---|---|---|
| Phase 1 — Data Foundation | Source, clean, and validate the master dataset (plants_master.csv) | Completed |
| Phase 2 — Application Build | Build the Streamlit recommendation app, feature engineering, and app-facing dataset (plants_app.csv) | Completed |
| Phase 3 — Deployment | Deploy the app publicly via Streamlit; document setup and local run instructions | Completed |
| Phase 4 — Documentation & Submission | Finalize README, written summary, walkthrough video; open submission PR | Completed |
| Phase 5 (Post-submission) — Expansion | Expand dataset coverage, add ML-based ranking, add mobile-responsive polish | Planned |

**Resources Needed**
- Public/open datasets (no licensing cost) from the four sources listed above
- Python data-processing stack (Pandas, NumPy) and Streamlit for the front end
- Team capacity across four disciplines (Data Analytics & UX/UI, Advanced Data Analytics, App Development & Automation, Cybersecurity) to cover data prep, app logic, deployment, and security review
- Streamlit Community Cloud (or equivalent) for hosting the live application

**Risks & Mitigations**

| Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Incomplete or inconsistent source data (species missing key fields) | Data quality report tracks and flags gaps; dataset was scoped down to well-documented species rather than the full raw species list to keep coverage high |
| Recommendations not matching real growing conditions in edge cases (e.g., microclimates) | Filtering logic is transparent and explainable so users can see why a plant was/wasn't recommended, and can be tuned as more data is validated |
| App downtime / hosting limits on free-tier deployment | Local run instructions are documented in the README as a fallback to the hosted app |
| Security exposure of a public-facing app (input handling, dependency vulnerabilities) | Dedicated cybersecurity review of the app's input handling and deployment configuration was built into the team workflow |
| Scope creep beyond submission deadline | Feature set was deliberately limited to a rule-based recommendation engine for this submission, with ML-based ranking and expanded data coverage deferred to "What's Next" |

